---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
import { USE_CASES } from '../../data/use-cases';
const path = '/use-cases';
const title = 'Shopify messaging journeys: choose the next operating task';
const desc = 'Start with the customer state that needs attention, then choose a playbook and define its entry, exit and evidence requirements.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">App procurement directory</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Unranked operating guide · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>Choose by the customer’s next action</h2>
    <p>A journey needs a reason to contact someone and a condition that makes the message obsolete. Use this map before selecting software. These are planning tasks, not merchant case studies or measured results.</p>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Starting state</th><th>Start here</th><th>Bring to the planning session</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>New permission, no order</td><td><a class="link" href="/use-cases/welcome-series">Welcome series</a></td><td>Capture promise, source and separate channel preferences</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Product interest, no checkout</td><td><a class="link" href="/use-cases/browse-abandonment">Browse abandonment</a></td><td>Identified product interest and permission to contact</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cart awaiting completion</td><td><a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Cart recovery</a></td><td>Cart identity, availability and purchase cancellation event</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Order placed</td><td><a class="link" href="/use-cases/post-purchase">Post-purchase</a></td><td>Delivery state, product education and support owner</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Repeat need or lapsed relationship</td><td><a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">Replenishment</a> / <a class="link" href="/use-cases/winback">winback</a></td><td>Usage assumptions, new orders and subscription state</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Time-limited demand</td><td><a class="link" href="/use-cases/product-launch">Launch</a> / <a class="link" href="/use-cases/back-in-stock">restock</a></td><td>Variant inventory, audience promise and expiry rule</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Seasonal pressure</td><td><a class="link" href="/use-cases/black-friday">Black Friday</a> / <a class="link" href="/use-cases/holiday-gifting">gifting</a></td><td>Offer calendar, shipping markets and service capacity</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>All journey and operating playbooks</h2>
    <p>The directory keeps every use-case route available. The cards describe jobs; they do not endorse the supplier lists or fixed timing assumptions in older individual guides. Set timing from your capture promise and operating constraints.</p>
    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      {USE_CASES.map((uc) => (<a class="card" href={`/use-cases/${uc.slug}`}><h3 class="capitalize">{uc.name}</h3><p>{uc.job}</p></a>))}
    </div>
    <h2>Write a journey contract</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Name one owner and one customer action. Record the triggering event and its required identifiers, timestamp and product fields.</li>
      <li>Specify entry eligibility independently for email and SMS. A product view or imported phone number does not itself establish promotional permission.</li>
      <li>Define expiry and cancellation: purchase, unavailable variant, resolved support issue, preference change or an expired offer.</li>
      <li>Assign priority when multiple journeys qualify. For example, a new purchase should cancel its old cart reminder before post-purchase education is queued.</li>
      <li>Record delivery-market scheduling requirements and the fallback when location or event data is missing. Route unresolved cases to review.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Rehearse collisions before enabling a journey</h2>
    <p>Use controlled test profiles to enter welcome and cart flows, then complete a purchase before the next queued message. Inspect both senders for the obsolete cart message. Repeat with a channel opt-out and an unavailable variant. Save event and queue evidence; this is a proposed rehearsal, not a claim that a vendor passed it.</p>
    <p>For a launch, check that early access and general release have distinct audiences and that sold-out variants remove their pending alerts. For replenishment, change the subscription state and reorder before the reminder. For gifting, check market-specific shipping cutoffs and keep recipient identity separate from purchaser identity.</p>
    <h2>Choose the supporting operating guide</h2>
    <p>Use <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">consent</a> for permission records, <a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">channel coordination</a> for ownership across senders, and <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a> for calendar priority. Resolve offer eligibility with <a class="link" href="/guides/offer-discipline">offer discipline</a>.</p>
    <h2>Measure the decision you changed</h2>
    <p>Choose a primary outcome per journey: completed carts, successful product education, fulfilled restock orders or repeat purchases. Keep a denominator of eligible customers, record exclusions and compare consistent observation windows. Where feasible, design a randomized holdout before launch; platform attribution alone does not establish incremental lift.</p>
    <p>Review contribution after product costs, discounts, refunds, sending charges and operating work. Track opt-outs, complaints and false alerts beside revenue. Use the <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">cost worksheet</a> with your actual quote. No universal send frequency or store-revenue threshold chooses a supplier for you.</p>
    <h2>Move from the journey to procurement</h2>
    <p>Take the event contract and rehearsal cases to the <a class="link" href="/apps">unranked app directory</a>. Ask shortlisted providers to demonstrate the exact journey, including exits and failure handling. Keep unresolved fields and ownership gaps in the acceptance record rather than treating a feature name as proof.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
